1
00:00:02,089 --> 00:00:04,439
[indistinct conversations]

2
00:00:12,577 --> 00:00:13,709
[gunshots]

3
00:00:13,796 --> 00:00:15,363
[crowd screaming]

4
00:00:17,669 --> 00:00:19,019
[thud]

5
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:38,473
[police radio chatter]

6
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:39,648
[police radio chatter]

7
00:00:42,651 --> 00:00:44,261
[siren wailing]

8
00:00:51,703 --> 00:00:53,096
[door opens]

9
00:00:59,624 --> 00:01:03,193
[sighs]

10
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,934
SO, PATRICK...

11
00:01:05,021 --> 00:01:06,892
THIS DOESN'T LOOK GOOD.

12
00:01:06,979 --> 00:01:10,722
TELL US YOUR SIDE OF THE STORY.
MAYBE WE CAN STRAIGHTEN IT OUT.

13
00:01:10,809 --> 00:01:14,987
IT'S A LONG STORY,
BUT, UH...

14
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,642
THE MAN I SHOT WAS RED JOHN.

15
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:20,558
SO YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT
YOU DID THAT. YOU KILLED HIM.

16
00:01:20,645 --> 00:01:22,995
YES, I DID.

17
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:27,130
CAN HARDLY DENY IT, CAN I?
500 WITNESSES.

18
00:01:28,523 --> 00:01:29,959
HE WAS RED JOHN.

19
00:01:30,046 --> 00:01:32,353
RED JOHN, THE FAMOUS
SERIAL KILLER? THAT RED JOHN?

20
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:34,746
YES. HE KILLED
MY WIFE AND DAUGHTER.

21
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:38,054
SO WHAT YOU DID, IN YOUR MIND,
IT WAS LIKE A RIGHTEOUS KILL.

22
00:01:38,141 --> 00:01:39,447
YES.

23
00:01:39,534 --> 00:01:41,231
HOW DID YOU KNOW IT WAS HIM?

24
00:01:41,318 --> 00:01:42,580
HE TOLD ME HE WAS.

25
00:01:42,667 --> 00:01:44,016
AND YOU BELIEVED HIM.

26
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:46,062
HE KNEW THINGS
ABOUT MY WIFE AND DAUGHTER

27
00:01:46,149 --> 00:01:48,020
THAT ONLY RED JOHN
WOULD KNOW.

28
00:01:48,108 --> 00:01:49,805
WHAT WAS THAT?

29
00:01:49,892 --> 00:01:52,329
HOW THEY SMELLED ON THE NIGHT
THAT HE KILLED THEM.

30
00:01:53,722 --> 00:01:55,941
OKAY.

31
00:01:56,028 --> 00:02:00,163
SO DID, UH, DID ANYONE ELSE
HEAR HIM SAY THIS TO YOU?NO.

32
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,992
YOU CAN ONLY ASSERT HE SAID
IT. YOU CAN'T PROVE IT.

33
00:02:03,079 --> 00:02:06,126
NO, I CAN'T, BUT THE GUN HE'S
CARRYING CERTAINLY BACKS ME UP.

34
00:02:06,213 --> 00:02:09,694
AND IF YOU CHECK HIS CELL PHONE,
HE RECEIVED A CALL AT 1:15

35
00:02:09,781 --> 00:02:12,436
FROM AN FBI AGENT
BY THE NAME OF CRAIG O'LAUGHLIN,

36
00:02:12,523 --> 00:02:16,832
WHO IS, WELL, WAS,
A PROVEN ACCOMPLICE OF RED JOHN.

37
00:02:16,919 --> 00:02:19,748
YOU TAKING ANY KIND
OF MEDICATION, PATRICK?

38
00:02:19,835 --> 00:02:21,619
NO.

39
00:02:21,706 --> 00:02:23,969
WHAT'S THAT GOT
TO DO WITH ANYTHING?

40
00:02:24,056 --> 00:02:26,972
HERE'S THE THING.
THAT'S A GREAT STORY YOU TELL.

41
00:02:27,059 --> 00:02:29,627
IF IT WAS TRUE, YOU COULD
PROBABLY ASK FOR MANSLAUGHTER,

42
00:02:29,714 --> 00:02:31,368
TAKE A 5-YEAR HIT, TOPS.

43
00:02:31,455 --> 00:02:32,630
IT IS TRUE.

44
00:02:32,717 --> 00:02:35,155
YEAH.
BUT THE PROBLEM IS, PATRICK,

45
00:02:35,242 --> 00:02:37,461
THE MAN YOU KILLED--
HIS NAME IS TIMOTHY CARTER.

46
00:02:37,548 --> 00:02:39,028
HE'S A WELL-RESPECTED
LOCAL BUSINESSMAN,

47
00:02:39,115 --> 00:02:41,596
A DEVOTED HUSBAND AND FATHER
WITH NO CRIMINAL RECORD.

48
00:02:41,683 --> 00:02:43,989
NO, THAT'S INCORRECT.WAIT A MINUTE.
LET ME FINISH.

49
00:02:44,076 --> 00:02:45,774
WE'VE ALREADY LOOKED
AT HIS CELL PHONE.

50
00:02:45,861 --> 00:02:47,341
I GOT THE DETAILS
RIGHT HERE.

51
00:02:47,428 --> 00:02:50,257
HE LOGGED ZERO CALLS
FROM THIS O'LAUGHLIN--

52
00:02:50,344 --> 00:02:51,997
NONE.

53
00:02:54,957 --> 00:02:56,306
[sighs] AND GUESS WHAT ELSE?

54
00:02:58,700 --> 00:03:01,311
HE DIDN'T HAVE A GUN ON HIM.

55
00:03:01,398 --> 00:03:03,226
NO GUN.

56
00:03:03,313 --> 00:03:05,707
NO GUN.

57
00:03:05,794 --> 00:03:08,405
[woman] SO YOU SEE
HOW THIS DOESN'T LOOK GOOD.

58
00:03:08,492 --> 00:03:10,886
LOOKS LIKE EITHER YOU'RE TELLING
US A PACK OF LIES,

59
00:03:10,973 --> 00:03:13,105
OR YOU WENT CRAZY

60
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:17,980
AND YOU KILLED AN INNOCENT MAN.

61
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:19,634
♪♪♪

62
00:03:31,472 --> 00:03:34,301
ARDILES.
HEY, I'M GLAD I CAUGHT YOU.

63
00:03:34,388 --> 00:03:36,085
JUST TO SAVE TIME HERE,
I'M SORRY,

64
00:03:36,172 --> 00:03:39,219
BUT I CAN'T CUT YOUR MAN JANE
ANY SLACK ON HIS BAIL.

65
00:03:39,306 --> 00:03:41,351
NO, NO.
I DON'T WANT YOU TO.

66
00:03:41,438 --> 00:03:43,179
NO, ON THE CONTRARY,
I WANT YOU

67
00:03:43,266 --> 00:03:46,530
TO MAKE SURE HE STAYS LOCKED UP
FOR AS LONG AS POSSIBLE.

68
00:03:46,617 --> 00:03:48,619
OKAY. HE'S YOUR MAN.

69
00:03:48,706 --> 00:03:51,405
WELL, DON'T GET ME WRONG--IT'S
HEARTBREAKING TO SEE A GOOD MAN

70
00:03:51,492 --> 00:03:54,582
AND A PRODUCTIVE EMPLOYEE
LIKE JANE GO DOWN IN FLAMES,

71
00:03:54,669 --> 00:03:56,845
BUT THIS IS ABOUT
DAMAGE CONTROL NOW.

72
00:03:56,932 --> 00:03:59,369
NEED TO MAKE SURE
HE IS OUT OF THE WAY

73
00:03:59,456 --> 00:04:02,154
UNTIL THIS MEDIA
CRAPSTORM PASSES.

74
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:05,201
UNDERSTOOD.

75
00:04:05,288 --> 00:04:06,724
YOUR HONOR,
THE DEFENDANT IS CHARGED

76
00:04:06,811 --> 00:04:08,726
WITH A HEINOUS
AND INEXPLICABLE CRIME

77
00:04:08,813 --> 00:04:10,728
THAT MAY ENTAIL
THE DEATH PENALTY.

78
00:04:10,815 --> 00:04:13,862
HE HAS NO TIES IN THE COMMUNITY,
HE OWNS NO PROPERTY HERE

79
00:04:13,949 --> 00:04:16,908
AND MUST BE CONSIDERED
A VERY SERIOUS FLIGHT RISK.

80
00:04:16,995 --> 00:04:21,304
I ASK THAT BAIL BE SET
AT A MINIMUM OF $1 MILLION.

81
00:04:21,391 --> 00:04:24,264
MR. JANE, ARE YOU SURE
ABOUT REPRESENTING YOURSELF?

82
00:04:24,351 --> 00:04:26,831
IT'S SELDOM A GOOD IDEA.

83
00:04:26,918 --> 00:04:31,488
I AM SURE, YOUR HONOR.
I APPRECIATE YOUR CONCERN.

84
00:04:31,575 --> 00:04:33,795
VERY WELL, THEN.
AS TO THE MATTER OF BAIL?

85
00:04:33,882 --> 00:04:36,624
OH, IT'S FINE.
NO--NO OBJECTION.

86
00:04:36,711 --> 00:04:40,236
REALLY? CAN YOU COME UP
WITH A MILLION DOLLARS?

87
00:04:40,323 --> 00:04:43,239
NO. I'M--I'M HAPPY
TO STAY IN JAIL FOR NOW.

88
00:04:43,326 --> 00:04:45,937
I-I NEED A LITTLE TIME
TO THINK ABOUT THINGS.

89
00:04:46,024 --> 00:04:48,026
WELL, THEN,
WE SHALL OBLIGE YOU.

90
00:04:48,113 --> 00:04:51,334
BAIL IS SET
AT A MILLION DOLLARS.

91
00:04:56,557 --> 00:04:58,646
[monitor beeping steadily]

92
00:04:59,821 --> 00:05:01,518
[door opens]

93
00:05:01,605 --> 00:05:02,693
[Bertram] AGENT LISBON.

94
00:05:06,393 --> 00:05:08,395
HOW ARE YOU?

95
00:05:08,482 --> 00:05:11,920
MM. PRETTY GOOD, CONSIDERING.

96
00:05:12,007 --> 00:05:14,139
PAINKILLERS ARE AMAZING
THESE DAYS, HUH?

97
00:05:14,226 --> 00:05:15,619
MM.

98
00:05:15,706 --> 00:05:17,099
HAVE YOU SEEN JANE?

99
00:05:17,186 --> 00:05:18,709
oh, ACROSS A COURTROOM.

100
00:05:18,796 --> 00:05:19,971
HOW WAS HE?

101
00:05:20,058 --> 00:05:21,495
WELL ENOUGH.

102
00:05:22,626 --> 00:05:24,106
I WANT TO EXTEND

103
00:05:24,193 --> 00:05:27,414
MY OWN AND THE BUREAU'S
DEEPEST SYMPATHIES TO YOU.

104
00:05:27,501 --> 00:05:28,980
THANK YOU.

105
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:32,288
DOCTOR SAYS I SHOULD BE
UP AND AROUND IN A DAY OR SO.

106
00:05:32,375 --> 00:05:35,509
OH, EXCELLENT.
EXCELLENT. BUT...

107
00:05:35,596 --> 00:05:40,209
D-DON'T RUSH YOUR RECOVERY.
YOU HAVE PLENTY OF TIME.

108
00:05:40,296 --> 00:05:43,865
YOU AND YOUR TEAM
ARE SUSPENDED AS OF TODAY.

109
00:05:43,952 --> 00:05:45,910
SUSPENDED.

110
00:05:45,997 --> 00:05:47,085
WHY?

111
00:05:47,172 --> 00:05:50,001
REALLY? YOU HAVE TO ASK?

112
00:05:50,088 --> 00:05:53,178
YOU ALLOWED
A CLEARLY DISTURBED INDIVIDUAL

113
00:05:53,265 --> 00:05:54,615
TO LEAD YOUR ACTIVITIES.

114
00:05:54,702 --> 00:05:57,357
YOU ALLOWED HIM
TO GUN DOWN AN INNOCENT MAN.

115
00:05:57,444 --> 00:05:58,532
WE DON'T KNOW THAT.

116
00:05:58,619 --> 00:05:59,924
AN INNOCENT MAN.

117
00:06:01,796 --> 00:06:05,930
ON TOP OF WHICH, YOU PERPETRATED
AN ELABORATE DECEPTION ON ME,

118
00:06:06,017 --> 00:06:08,759
IN ORDER TO GATHER EVIDENCE
THAT I, YOUR OWN BOSS,

119
00:06:08,846 --> 00:06:11,849
AM PART OF
A VAST CRIMINAL CONSPIRACY.

120
00:06:11,936 --> 00:06:13,111
SHALL I GO ON?

121
00:06:13,198 --> 00:06:14,896
BUT YOU CAN'T DO THIS.
PLEASE, YOU--

122
00:06:14,983 --> 00:06:17,377
SHH, STAY CALM, LISBON.

123
00:06:17,464 --> 00:06:20,467
FOCUS ON GETTING WELL.

124
00:06:20,554 --> 00:06:23,861
WE'LL REVISIT YOUR STATUS
WHEN YOU'RE FULLY RECOVERED.

125
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:29,606
BUT WHAT ABOUT JANE?

126
00:06:31,869 --> 00:06:33,567
FORGET ABOUT JANE.

127
00:06:42,532 --> 00:06:44,099
NURSE?

128
00:06:44,186 --> 00:06:47,494
[moans]

129
00:06:47,581 --> 00:06:48,538
[indistinct conversations]

130
00:06:54,675 --> 00:06:57,025
[door buzzes]

131
00:07:10,473 --> 00:07:11,779
SO HOW WAS YOUR WEEK?

132
00:07:11,866 --> 00:07:13,520
[laughs]

133
00:07:13,607 --> 00:07:15,565
OH, YOU SHOULD BE
IN THE HOSPITAL.

134
00:07:15,652 --> 00:07:16,958
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

135
00:07:17,045 --> 00:07:19,482
I'M OKAY.
YOU, ON THE OTHER HAND...

136
00:07:19,569 --> 00:07:21,397
OH, I'M OKAY, TOO.

137
00:07:21,484 --> 00:07:25,270
YOU KILLED AN UNARMED MAN
IN FRONT OF 500 WITNESSES.

138
00:07:25,357 --> 00:07:26,402
YOU'RE NOT OKAY.

139
00:07:26,489 --> 00:07:28,143
HE HAD A GUN.

140
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:31,102
SOMEONE MUST HAVE TAKEN IT
AND SWITCHED THE CELL PHONE.

141
00:07:31,189 --> 00:07:33,104
IT'S THE ONLY
POSSIBLE EXPLANATION.

142
00:07:33,191 --> 00:07:37,065
THAT, OR YOU WENT NUTS
FOR A MOMENT.

143
00:07:37,152 --> 00:07:38,501
LISBON, LOOK AT ME.

144
00:07:40,547 --> 00:07:42,679
I DIDN'T GO NUTS.

145
00:07:42,766 --> 00:07:45,073
I BELIEVE YOU.

146
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,596
I'M NOT SURE A JURY WILL.

147
00:07:46,683 --> 00:07:48,511
YEAH, WELL,
THAT IS A PROBLEM,

148
00:07:48,598 --> 00:07:54,604
BUT I DID WHAT I HAD TO DO, AND
I'LL LIVE WITH THE CONSEQUENCES.

149
00:07:54,691 --> 00:07:57,999
NEXT TIME YOU COME, CAN YOU
BRING SOME BLUEBERRY MUFFINS?

150
00:08:00,871 --> 00:08:02,525
HEY, GUYS.

151
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,537
GRACE, YOU DIDN'T
HAVE TO COME IN.

152
00:08:14,624 --> 00:08:16,147
WE COULD HAVE GOTTEN
YOUR STUFF.

153
00:08:16,234 --> 00:08:18,149
OH, IT'S NO BIG DEAL.

154
00:08:18,236 --> 00:08:19,890
OKAY.

155
00:08:19,977 --> 00:08:23,024
UM, HOW ARE YOU DOING?
YOU GOOD?

156
00:08:23,111 --> 00:08:24,895
YEAH, I'M FINE.

157
00:08:24,982 --> 00:08:28,029
TWO DAYS AGO YOU SHOT
YOUR FIANCE. YOU CAN'T BE FINE.

158
00:08:28,116 --> 00:08:29,378
JEEZ, CHO.WHAT?

159
00:08:29,465 --> 00:08:31,206
YOU NEED TO SPELL IT OUT?

160
00:08:31,293 --> 00:08:32,512
LOOK, I AM PERFECTLY FINE,

161
00:08:32,599 --> 00:08:35,689
AND I DON'T WANT
TO TALK ABOUT IT. OKAY?

162
00:08:35,776 --> 00:08:37,299
HEY, BOSS.

163
00:08:37,386 --> 00:08:38,822
AREN'T YOU SUPPOSED
TO BE HOSPITAL?

164
00:08:38,909 --> 00:08:39,954
NEVER MIND THAT.

165
00:08:40,041 --> 00:08:42,565
BUT YOU SHOULD BE--I'M FINE.

166
00:08:42,652 --> 00:08:46,003
WE NEED TO WORK ON DIGGING
OURSELVES AND JANE OUT OF THIS.

167
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:47,744
HOW DO WE DO THAT?

168
00:08:47,831 --> 00:08:50,530
FIRST, WE PROVE THAT THIS
TIMOTHY CARTER GUY WAS RED JOHN.

169
00:08:50,617 --> 00:08:52,793
HARD TO DO.
HOW DO WE WORK WITHOUT BADGES?

170
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:54,708
IT BREAKS THE TERMS
OF OUR SUSPENSION.

171
00:08:54,795 --> 00:08:58,668
YES, BUT I DON'T SEE THAT WE
HAVE ANY OTHER CHOICES. YOU IN?

172
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:03,368
YES.

173
00:09:07,024 --> 00:09:08,591
GRACE, WHAT AM I THINKING?

174
00:09:08,678 --> 00:09:10,462
YOU NEED TO GO HOME AND REST.

175
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,987
THE GUYS AND I CAN MANAGE THIS
TO START WITH.

176
00:09:13,074 --> 00:09:14,728
SERIOUSLY, I'M TOTALLY OKAY.

177
00:09:14,815 --> 00:09:17,948
NO. YOU NEED TO GO HOME
AND TAKE IT EASY.

178
00:09:18,035 --> 00:09:19,559
I CAN'T GO HOME.

179
00:09:21,299 --> 00:09:23,911
I NEED TO WORK.
I NEED TO BE AROUND PEOPLE.

180
00:09:23,998 --> 00:09:26,261
[clatter, rustle]

181
00:09:27,828 --> 00:09:30,047
YOU'RE RIGHT.
I CAN'T TELL YOU WHAT TO DO.

182
00:09:30,134 --> 00:09:33,529
YOU WANT TO STAY, STAY.
WE'D LOVE TO HAVE YOU.

183
00:09:36,358 --> 00:09:39,361
YOU GUYS WANT TO FOCUS ON
FINDING THE GUN AND CELL PHONE?

184
00:09:39,448 --> 00:09:42,451
ASSUME IT WAS TAKEN BEFORE SAC
P.D. AND FORENSICS GOT THERE?

185
00:09:42,538 --> 00:09:44,496
WE NEED TO LOOK
AT THE SECURITY VIDEO.

186
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,803
WHO TOOK THE EVIDENCE
HAS TO BE ON CAMERA.

187
00:09:46,890 --> 00:09:49,501
WE'LL CHECK OUT TIMOTHY CARTER.
IF HE WAS RED JOHN

188
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:51,286
HE WOULD'VE LEFT
EVIDENCE OF IT SOMEPLACE.

189
00:09:51,373 --> 00:09:52,548
IFHE WAS RED JOHN.

190
00:09:52,635 --> 00:09:56,421
HE WAS.
JANE DID NOT GO CRAZY.

191
00:09:56,508 --> 00:09:58,423
[door slams]

192
00:09:58,510 --> 00:10:01,383
[clanking,
indistinct conversations]

193
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:17,965
[Rigsby] HI.

194
00:10:18,052 --> 00:10:20,750
REMEMBER US? WERE AT THE
STAKEOUT THAT LED
TO THE SHOOTING?

195
00:10:20,837 --> 00:10:23,535
OH, YEAH. THAT WAS
SOME SITUATION, HUH?

196
00:10:23,623 --> 00:10:25,189
[chuckles]
HOW CAN I HELP YOU?

197
00:10:25,276 --> 00:10:27,496
WE NEED TO SEE THAT DAY'S
VIDEO SURVEILLANCE FOOTAGE.

198
00:10:27,583 --> 00:10:29,803
OF COURSE, SURE.
UH, WE GOT IT ON DISK,

199
00:10:29,890 --> 00:10:32,893
OR I CAN DOWNLOAD IT
AND E-MAIL YOU.DISK WOULD BE FINE.

200
00:10:32,980 --> 00:10:34,677
NO PROBLEMO.JUST SHOW ME THE WARRANT.

201
00:10:34,764 --> 00:10:37,201
I'LL GET RIGHT ON IT.WE'LL SEND YOU THE WARRANT.

202
00:10:37,288 --> 00:10:39,508
WE'RE KIND OF IN A HURRY HERE.I BET.

203
00:10:39,595 --> 00:10:42,598
MUST BE ALL KINDS
OF CRAP FLYING OVER THIS.

204
00:10:42,685 --> 00:10:46,123
[chuckles] YOUR GUY REALLY
GOT HIS BRONSON ON, HUH? BOOM.

205
00:10:46,210 --> 00:10:47,516
YEAH.

206
00:10:47,603 --> 00:10:48,822
WILD.

207
00:10:48,909 --> 00:10:50,867
I NEED TO SEE
THE WARRANT FIRST, THOUGH.

208
00:10:50,954 --> 00:10:52,695
IT'S, UH, IT'S PROTOCOL.

209
00:10:52,782 --> 00:10:55,176
THERE IS NO WARRANT.

210
00:10:57,395 --> 00:10:58,919
ASK ME WHY.WHY?

211
00:10:59,006 --> 00:11:01,443
BECAUSE EVERY MEMBER OF OUR UNIT
IS SUSPENDED, BECAUSE OF

212
00:11:01,530 --> 00:11:05,186
THIS KILLING HERE AND TWO OTHER
PEOPLE WE KILLED THIS WEEK.

213
00:11:07,231 --> 00:11:09,364
WOW, THAT'S, UH...

214
00:11:09,451 --> 00:11:11,148
ROUGH WEEK.

215
00:11:11,235 --> 00:11:15,544
[clears throat] UH, I GUESS
I CAN RUN YOU OFF A COPY.

216
00:11:15,631 --> 00:11:17,415
THAT'D BE GREAT.
THANK YOU.

217
00:11:17,502 --> 00:11:18,852
[typing on keyboard]

218
00:11:18,939 --> 00:11:20,592
[bicycle bell jingles]

219
00:11:21,811 --> 00:11:24,205
[car door slams]

220
00:11:28,339 --> 00:11:29,863
[knock on door]

221
00:11:32,343 --> 00:11:33,954
HELLO?

222
00:11:34,041 --> 00:11:36,565
MRS. CARTER? I'M TERESA LISBON.
THIS IS GRACE VAN PELT.

223
00:11:38,045 --> 00:11:40,917
WE'RE COLLEAGUES OF PATRICK JANE
FROM THE CBI.

224
00:11:41,004 --> 00:11:44,834
OH. OH.YES?

225
00:11:44,921 --> 00:11:47,794
WE'D VERY MUCH TO SPEAK WITH YOU
IF THAT'S POSSIBLE.

226
00:11:47,881 --> 00:11:51,058
UM...

227
00:11:51,145 --> 00:11:54,931
YES. ALRIGHT.
PLEASE, COME IN.

228
00:11:56,933 --> 00:12:00,371
THIS IS REVEREND FARLEY
AND MY FRIEND JOAN.

229
00:12:00,458 --> 00:12:03,157
THESE ARE COLLEAGUES
OF PATRICK JANE.

230
00:12:03,244 --> 00:12:04,158
[gasps]JANE?

231
00:12:04,245 --> 00:12:06,029
YES.

232
00:12:06,116 --> 00:12:07,857
I'M NOT SURE
IF THIS IS APPROPRIATE.

233
00:12:07,944 --> 00:12:11,295
NO, THAT'S ALRIGHT.
I'M HAPPY TO TALK WITH THEM.

234
00:12:11,382 --> 00:12:12,862
WELL, IF THAT'S THE CASE,

235
00:12:12,949 --> 00:12:15,647
WE'LL TAKE CHARLAINE
OUT TO PLAY, SHALL WE?

236
00:12:15,735 --> 00:12:17,171
GIVE YOU A MOMENT.

237
00:12:17,258 --> 00:12:19,739
[whispers] THANK YOU.

238
00:12:21,915 --> 00:12:24,700
CAN I OFFER YOU
SOME COFFEE OR TEA?

239
00:12:24,787 --> 00:12:26,833
COFFEE WOULD BE GREAT,
THANK YOU.

240
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:29,749
THIS MUST BE
A TERRIBLE TIME FOR YOU,

241
00:12:29,836 --> 00:12:33,100
AND I'M SURE YOU HAVE
A LOT OF QUESTIONS.

242
00:12:36,843 --> 00:12:39,628
BUT...

243
00:12:39,715 --> 00:12:42,457
I CAN TELL YOU RIGHT NOW

244
00:12:42,544 --> 00:12:45,590
THAT MY HUSBAND WAS NOT
THIS RED JOHN PERSON.

245
00:12:48,202 --> 00:12:49,725
HE WAS...

246
00:12:49,812 --> 00:12:52,032
THE KINDEST...

247
00:12:52,119 --> 00:12:54,774
GENTLEST SOUL YOU CAN IMAGINE,

248
00:12:54,861 --> 00:12:55,775
AND...

249
00:12:55,862 --> 00:12:59,909
I DON'T KNOW HOW...

250
00:12:59,996 --> 00:13:04,914
BUT YOUR COLLEAGUE MADE
A TERRIBLE, TERRIBLE MISTAKE.

251
00:13:05,001 --> 00:13:07,699
IS IT POSSIBLE YOUR HUSBAND
HID THINGS FROM YOU?

252
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:09,266
OTHER ASPECTS OF HIS LIFE?

253
00:13:09,353 --> 00:13:12,182
WE WERE VERY CLOSE.

254
00:13:12,269 --> 00:13:15,011
WE DIDN'T KEEP SECRETS
FROM EACH OTHER, EVER.

255
00:13:15,098 --> 00:13:16,796
HOW DO YOU KNOW?

256
00:13:16,883 --> 00:13:19,015
EXCUSE ME?

257
00:13:19,102 --> 00:13:20,625
I MEAN, A SECRET,
BY DEFINITION,

258
00:13:20,712 --> 00:13:22,497
IS SOMETHING
YOU DON'T KNOW, RIGHT?

259
00:13:26,066 --> 00:13:27,371
HOW LONG WERE YOU MARRIED?

260
00:13:29,069 --> 00:13:32,289
THREE YEARS THIS FRIDAY.

261
00:13:32,376 --> 00:13:36,163
HE WAS AT THAT MALL,
BUYING AN ANNIVERSARY GIFT.

262
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:38,643
SO HE WAS THE PERFECT MAN.

263
00:13:38,730 --> 00:13:40,689
NOBODY'S PERFECT.

264
00:13:42,865 --> 00:13:47,609
[voice breaking]
HE IS A GOOD MAN.

265
00:13:47,696 --> 00:13:49,437
WAS.

266
00:13:51,004 --> 00:13:52,396
ONLY LAST MONTH,

267
00:13:52,483 --> 00:13:55,008
HE GOT AN OFFICIAL COMMENDATION
FROM THE SHERIFF.

268
00:13:55,095 --> 00:13:56,357
FOR WHAT?

269
00:13:56,444 --> 00:13:59,403
WHEN DEBBI LUBIN WENT MISSING,

270
00:13:59,490 --> 00:14:02,145
TIM ORGANIZED
THE VOLUNTEER SEARCH PARTIES.

271
00:14:02,232 --> 00:14:03,581
WHO'S DEBBI LUBIN?

272
00:14:03,668 --> 00:14:08,195
OH, UM,
A GIRL FROM OUR CHURCH.

273
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:11,198
SHE WENT MISSING ABOUT...
[sniffles]

274
00:14:11,285 --> 00:14:15,724
SIX WEEKS AGO. POOR THING.

275
00:14:15,811 --> 00:14:17,857
ONLY 17.

276
00:14:17,944 --> 00:14:19,815
[Van Pelt]
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

277
00:14:19,902 --> 00:14:21,643
I DON'T KNOW.
SHE SEEMED SINCERE.

278
00:14:21,730 --> 00:14:23,166
HOUSE IS CLEAN AS A WHISTLE.

279
00:14:23,253 --> 00:14:25,212
HE MUST HAVE KEPT A HIDEOUT
SOMEPLACE ELSE.

280
00:14:25,299 --> 00:14:26,996
[scoffs]
I THINK SHE'S FULL OF IT.

281
00:14:27,083 --> 00:14:29,607
YEAH, YOU MADE THAT PLAIN.
LISTEN, GRACE,

282
00:14:29,694 --> 00:14:33,002
YOU NEED TO SIGN UP FOR YOUR
COUNSELING SESSIONS A.S.A.P.

283
00:14:33,089 --> 00:14:35,265
[scoffs] SESSIONS? WITH
THE SHRINK? I DON'T NEED IT.

284
00:14:35,352 --> 00:14:37,006
WELL, I THINK YOU DO.

285
00:14:37,093 --> 00:14:40,792
BESIDES, IT'S NOT YOUR CALL.
IT'S MANDATORY AFTER A SHOOTING.

286
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,056
THEY SAY A PSYCH COUNSELING
SHEET IN YOUR FILE

287
00:14:43,143 --> 00:14:44,535
DOESN'T MATTER, BUT IT DOES.

288
00:14:44,622 --> 00:14:48,409
GRACE, I'M ASKING YOU
AS A FRIEND. GET HELP.

289
00:14:48,496 --> 00:14:51,325
SEE THE SHRINK.
TALK ABOUT WHAT HAPPENED.

290
00:14:51,412 --> 00:14:53,066
DON'T LET THIS
EAT AWAY AT YOU.

291
00:14:54,806 --> 00:14:58,898
I APPRECIATE THE CONCERN,
REALLY. THANK YOU.

292
00:15:01,770 --> 00:15:03,815
LISTEN, WE'VE GOT
A SERIOUS PROBLEM.

293
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:05,600
WAS REALLY LOOKING FORWARD
TO A MUFFIN.

294
00:15:05,687 --> 00:15:07,863
TIMOTHY CARTER
LOOKS INNOCENT.

295
00:15:07,950 --> 00:15:11,258
HIS WIFE MAKES A GOOD CASE
FOR HIM. HIS HOUSE WAS CLEAN.

296
00:15:11,345 --> 00:15:12,912
YOU SEARCH THE WHOLE PLACE?

297
00:15:12,999 --> 00:15:14,870
WE DIDN'T RIP OUT
THE FLOORBOARDS.

298
00:15:14,957 --> 00:15:16,654
SURE, HE COULD HAVE
BEEN HIDING SOMETHING,

299
00:15:16,741 --> 00:15:18,134
BUT WITHOUT ANY CLUES,

300
00:15:18,221 --> 00:15:20,571
WE DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHERE TO START LOOKING.

301
00:15:20,658 --> 00:15:23,009
WHAT'S CARTER'S STORY?
WHERE'S HE FROM?

302
00:15:23,096 --> 00:15:25,620
ONLY CHILD OF MISSIONARIES,
GREW UP IN AFRICA,

303
00:15:25,707 --> 00:15:27,187
STUDIED AND LIVED ABROAD

304
00:15:27,274 --> 00:15:29,972
UNTIL HE MOVED TO THE U.S.
TO LIVE IN '06.

305
00:15:30,059 --> 00:15:32,583
SO IN OTHER WORDS,
HE JUST APPEARS ON THE GRID

306
00:15:32,670 --> 00:15:35,238
FIVE YEARS AGO. THAT SOUNDS
LIKE A FAKE IDENTITY.

307
00:15:35,325 --> 00:15:38,589
MAYBE. OR HE'S A GUY WHO MOVED
TO THE COUNTRY FIVE YEARS AGO.

308
00:15:38,676 --> 00:15:41,679
THE ONLY RED FLAG WE HAVE
IS THAT HE RECENTLY PUT HIMSELF

309
00:15:41,766 --> 00:15:44,769
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE SEARCH FOR
A GIRL WHO'S GONE MISSING.

310
00:15:44,856 --> 00:15:46,510
THAT'S YOUR CLASSIC
ORGANIZED CRIMINAL

311
00:15:46,597 --> 00:15:49,905
PSYCHOPATH BEHAVIOR--INSERTING
HIMSELF INTO AN INVESTIGATION.

312
00:15:49,992 --> 00:15:54,040
AGAIN, MAYBE. OR HE'S A GOOD GUY
WHO WANTS TO DO THE RIGHT THING.

313
00:15:54,127 --> 00:15:57,173
WE HAVE NO HARD FACTS,
JUST YOUR WORD.

314
00:15:57,260 --> 00:16:00,872
AND YOU'RE BEGINNING TO THINK
THAT MAYBE MY WORD IS DUBIOUS.

315
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,223
MAYBE I'M CRAZY.

316
00:16:03,310 --> 00:16:05,616
MAYBE I SHOT SOME RANDOM GUY.

317
00:16:05,703 --> 00:16:07,314
NO.

318
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:12,058
IT'S CROSSED MY MIND, YEAH.

319
00:16:12,145 --> 00:16:13,276
FAIR ENOUGH.

320
00:16:15,322 --> 00:16:18,325
GUESS I'M GONNA HAVE TO GET OUT
TO HELP YOU WITH THIS.

321
00:16:18,412 --> 00:16:21,632
HOW? YOUR BAIL'S SET
AT A MILLION BUCKS.YEAH, THAT'S NO PROBLEM.

322
00:16:21,719 --> 00:16:24,896
ONCE I GET THE MONEY,
I'LL CALL YOU.HOW YOU GONNA DO THAT?

323
00:16:24,984 --> 00:16:26,115
I'LL THINK OF SOMETHING.

324
00:16:26,202 --> 00:16:27,943
MEANTIME, I NEED YOU
TO GET AHOLD

325
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:30,641
OF TIMOTHY CARTER'S
PERSONAL EFFECTS FROM FORENSICS.

326
00:16:30,728 --> 00:16:32,426
HOW AM I GONNA DO THAT?

327
00:16:32,513 --> 00:16:34,732
YOU'LL THINK OF SOMETHING.

328
00:16:34,819 --> 00:16:37,822
[screaming]

329
00:16:37,909 --> 00:16:41,087
JANE SAYS THE GUN
WAS IN THE NEWSPAPER.

330
00:16:41,174 --> 00:16:42,871
[keys tap]

331
00:16:42,958 --> 00:16:43,915
[Cho] THERE.

332
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,091
LOOKS LIKE A WAITRESS.

333
00:16:45,178 --> 00:16:46,831
CAN'T SEE
IF SHE TAKES ANYTHING.

334
00:16:46,918 --> 00:16:48,703
[keys tap]

335
00:16:48,790 --> 00:16:50,357
SECURITY GUARD.

336
00:16:50,444 --> 00:16:52,272
[tap]

337
00:16:52,359 --> 00:16:56,102
[Rigsby]
AND THAT'S THE FORENSIC TECH.

338
00:16:56,189 --> 00:16:57,494
NO GUN.

339
00:16:57,581 --> 00:16:59,322
ONE OF THOSE THREE
MUST'VE TAKEN IT--

340
00:16:59,409 --> 00:17:00,976
WAITRESS, SECURITY GUARD,
FORENSIC TECH.

341
00:17:01,063 --> 00:17:02,499
YEAH, IF THERE WASA GUN.

342
00:17:04,588 --> 00:17:05,720
[Rigsby] YEAH.

343
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:08,288
[indistinct conversations]

344
00:17:10,812 --> 00:17:13,032
[man speaking indistinctly over P.A.]

345
00:17:22,911 --> 00:17:25,392
I LOVE A GOOD GAME OF CARDS.
WHAT'S THE BUY-IN?

346
00:17:25,479 --> 00:17:27,611
BUY-IN'S 100 GRAND,
OUTSIDE MONEY.

347
00:17:27,698 --> 00:17:29,309
EXCELLENT. I'M IN.

348
00:17:29,396 --> 00:17:30,788
YOU GOT TO HAVE COLLATERAL,

349
00:17:30,875 --> 00:17:32,834
SO WE KNOW
YOU CAN COVER YOUR DEBTS.

350
00:17:32,921 --> 00:17:34,879
NO PROBLEM.
I GOT ALL SORTS OF COLLATERAL.

351
00:17:34,966 --> 00:17:38,709
I HAVE A VINTAGE CAR COLLECTION
WORTH 2 1/2 MIL OR THEREABOUTS.

352
00:17:38,796 --> 00:17:40,276
HOW DO WE KNOW THAT?

353
00:17:40,363 --> 00:17:43,018
WELL, WHAT KIND OF FOOL
WOULD LIE TO FOLKS LIKE YOU

354
00:17:43,105 --> 00:17:44,889
ABOUT SOMETHIN' LIKE THAT?

355
00:17:44,976 --> 00:17:48,806
IF YOU FOUND OUT I WAS LYING,
YOU'D KILL ME, RIGHT?

356
00:17:48,893 --> 00:17:50,765
TRUE. TAKE A SEAT.

357
00:17:50,852 --> 00:17:52,419
THANK YOU.

358
00:17:53,898 --> 00:17:55,770
[clears throat]

359
00:17:55,857 --> 00:17:57,728
I WAS THE FIRST TECH
ON SCENE.

360
00:17:57,815 --> 00:18:00,992
SPOKE TO THE DETECTIVES
FROM SAC P.D.YOU KNOW.

361
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,733
THERE'S MULTIPLE INVESTIGATIONS
GOING ON HERE.

362
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:05,562
OH, SURE. BUT AREN'T
YOU GUYS SUSPENDED?

363
00:18:05,649 --> 00:18:07,956
TECHNICALLY, YEAH,
BUT WE'RE JUST TALKING HERE.

364
00:18:08,043 --> 00:18:10,915
I'M NOT SURE I SHOULD BE...
TALKING TO YOU.

365
00:18:11,002 --> 00:18:12,787
WHY NOT? YOU HAVE
SOMETHING TO HIDE?

366
00:18:12,874 --> 00:18:15,398
NO. WHAT WOULD I BE HIDING?

367
00:18:15,485 --> 00:18:17,096
LOOK.

368
00:18:17,183 --> 00:18:20,186
SOMEONE TOOK A CELL PHONE
AND A GUN FROM THE CRIME SCENE.

369
00:18:20,273 --> 00:18:22,797
NOT ME. THERE WAS NO GUN,
NOT THAT I SAW.

370
00:18:22,884 --> 00:18:24,190
WAIT.

371
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,976
LOOK ME IN THE EYE
AND TELL ME THAT.

372
00:18:28,063 --> 00:18:30,631
THERE WAS NO GUN.

373
00:18:34,591 --> 00:18:37,551
[indistinct conversations]

374
00:18:39,466 --> 00:18:41,032
25.

375
00:18:42,773 --> 00:18:44,558
[whistles]

376
00:18:48,301 --> 00:18:53,001
OKAY, WELL, I'M GONNA SEE YOU,
AND THEN I WILL RAISE YOU...

377
00:18:58,267 --> 00:18:59,790
ALL IN.

378
00:19:03,925 --> 00:19:05,840
[clears throat]

379
00:19:07,711 --> 00:19:10,975
YOU KNOW, PUSS...

380
00:19:11,062 --> 00:19:15,806
WHEN YOU BLUFF,
YOU HAVE A REAL OBVIOUS TELL.

381
00:19:15,893 --> 00:19:18,548
WHEN I REACH TO TUG ON MY EAR,
BUT STOP MYSELF?

382
00:19:18,635 --> 00:19:20,681
YEAH.

383
00:19:20,768 --> 00:19:25,773
OH. OHH, BAM. STRAIGHT FLUSH.
HE GOT YOU GOOD.

384
00:19:25,860 --> 00:19:28,515
[laughs]

385
00:19:28,602 --> 00:19:29,994
[snorts]

386
00:19:32,475 --> 00:19:34,477
[tires screech]

387
00:19:50,667 --> 00:19:52,321
TERESA LISBON?

388
00:19:52,408 --> 00:19:55,411
YES?

389
00:19:55,498 --> 00:19:59,894
PHIL SAYS TO TELL YOUR FRIEND HE
DOESN'T WANT TO SEE HIM AGAIN.

390
00:20:18,434 --> 00:20:19,566
HI.

391
00:20:19,653 --> 00:20:21,263
HEY.

392
00:20:25,659 --> 00:20:28,705
SO WHAT DID YOU DO,
HONESTLY?

393
00:20:28,792 --> 00:20:30,229
HE HAD A GUN.

394
00:20:30,316 --> 00:20:32,840
NO, I MEAN, HOW DID YOU
RAISE THE BAIL MONEY?

395
00:20:32,927 --> 00:20:35,495
OH, THAT.
UH, MURDER FOR HIRE.

396
00:20:35,582 --> 00:20:37,671
KILLED A SNITCH.
STABBED HIM IN THE KIDNEYS.

397
00:20:37,758 --> 00:20:38,889
YOU DID NOT.

398
00:20:38,976 --> 00:20:40,456
I DID NOT.

399
00:20:40,543 --> 00:20:44,155
I WON IT IN A CARD GAME,
BUT I HAD YOU FOR A MOMENT.

400
00:20:44,243 --> 00:20:46,375
YOU REALLY DO
FEAR FOR MY SANITY.

401
00:20:46,462 --> 00:20:48,638
NO. WHAT DO WE DO NOW?

402
00:20:48,725 --> 00:20:51,989
WELL, FIRST, EGGS.
THEN WE GO SEE SALLY CARTER.

403
00:20:52,076 --> 00:20:54,253
DID YOU GET HER HUSBAND'S
EFFECTS FROM FORENSICS?

404
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:56,472
YES. I HAD TO LIE
THROUGH MY TEETH,

405
00:20:56,559 --> 00:20:59,519
CALL IN ALL KINDS OF FAVORS,
AND IT WAS A BUST.

406
00:20:59,606 --> 00:21:02,826
NOTHING USEFUL.
WATCH, KEY, GUM, WEDDING RING.

407
00:21:02,913 --> 00:21:06,090
DOESN'T MATTER. GETS US
IN THE ROOM WITH SALLY CARTER.

408
00:21:06,177 --> 00:21:08,354
I DON'T THINK SHE'S GONNA
WANNA TALK TO YOU.

409
00:21:08,441 --> 00:21:09,529
REALLY?

410
00:21:09,616 --> 00:21:11,226
YOU KILLED HER HUSBAND.

411
00:21:11,313 --> 00:21:13,446
WELL, THERE YOU GO.
THE ICE IS BROKEN.

412
00:21:13,533 --> 00:21:15,796
WE HAVE SOMETHING
TO TALK ABOUT.

413
00:21:25,371 --> 00:21:27,808
NO, HE DIDN'T HAVE A GUN,
NOT THAT I SAW.

414
00:21:27,895 --> 00:21:30,289
DID YOU NOTICE THE NEWSPAPER
THAT HE WAS CARRYING?

415
00:21:30,376 --> 00:21:32,465
NO. I DIDN'T REALLY
SEE ANYTHING.

416
00:21:32,552 --> 00:21:34,945
I WAS TRYING TO
COMFORT HIM THE BEST I COULD.

417
00:21:35,032 --> 00:21:37,078
SO HE WAS STILL ALIVE.

418
00:21:37,165 --> 00:21:38,775
YES.DID HE SAY ANYTHING?

419
00:21:38,862 --> 00:21:42,562
HE SAID, "GIVE MY LOVE
TO SALLY AND CHARLAINE."

420
00:21:42,649 --> 00:21:43,650
THAT'S ALL?

421
00:21:43,737 --> 00:21:45,129
THEN HE DIED.

422
00:21:45,216 --> 00:21:47,175
I THINK, ANYHOW.
HE DIDN'T SAY ANYTHING ELSE,

423
00:21:47,262 --> 00:21:49,438
AND THE SECURITY GUARD
WAS FREAKING OUT AT ME,

424
00:21:49,525 --> 00:21:50,831
SO I LEFT HIM.

425
00:21:50,918 --> 00:21:52,441
WHY WAS THE GUARD
FREAKING OUT?

426
00:21:52,528 --> 00:21:55,314
HE WAS LIKE,
"GET AWAY FROM THE BODY!

427
00:21:55,401 --> 00:21:57,272
THIS IS EVIDENCE!
DON'T TOUCH HIM!"

428
00:21:57,359 --> 00:21:59,361
HE WAS KIND OF
A JERK ABOUT IT.

429
00:21:59,448 --> 00:22:01,450
THIS GUARD--
HE WAS A YOUNGISH BALD GUY?

430
00:22:01,537 --> 00:22:04,540
YES, WITH CRAZY EYES.

431
00:22:04,627 --> 00:22:07,021
[man] YEAH, RON DEUTSCH.

432
00:22:07,108 --> 00:22:10,590
HE WAS SUPPOSED TO BE WORKING
TODAY, BUT HE DIDN'T SHOW UP.

433
00:22:10,677 --> 00:22:12,287
I NEED HIS HOME ADDRESS.

434
00:22:13,506 --> 00:22:15,072
[sighs]

435
00:22:17,118 --> 00:22:19,468
[types on keyboard]

436
00:22:25,387 --> 00:22:27,215
[doorbell rings]

437
00:22:27,302 --> 00:22:29,260
I HAVE A BAD FEELING
ABOUT THIS.

438
00:22:29,348 --> 00:22:32,438
WELL, YOU'VE BEEN SHOT. YOU'RE
BOUND TO HAVE A GLOOMY OUTLOOK.

439
00:22:32,525 --> 00:22:33,743
IGNORE YOUR FEELINGS.

440
00:22:37,486 --> 00:22:40,010
I'M SORRY, AGENTS.
THIS ISN'T A GOOD TIME.

441
00:22:40,097 --> 00:22:42,273
WE'RE HAVING
A SMALL MEMORIAL PARTY FOR TIM.

442
00:22:42,361 --> 00:22:44,145
WE HAVE
HIS PERSONAL EFFECTS HERE.

443
00:22:44,232 --> 00:22:45,886
THANK YOU.
I CAN TAKE THOSE.

444
00:22:45,973 --> 00:22:48,932
I'M SORRY. MRS. CARTER HAS TO
SIGN FOR THEM IN OUR PRESENCE.

445
00:22:49,019 --> 00:22:50,325
SHOULDN'T TAKE LONG.

446
00:22:50,412 --> 00:22:54,547
I SEE. UH, LET'S GO AROUND
TO THE KITCHEN DOOR.

447
00:22:54,634 --> 00:22:57,027
OKAY, THEN.

448
00:22:57,114 --> 00:22:58,681
GOT TO GO.

449
00:22:58,768 --> 00:22:59,943
[cell phone shuts]

450
00:23:00,030 --> 00:23:02,642
[indistinct conversations]

451
00:23:02,729 --> 00:23:04,295
WELL, THIS IS EASY AS PIE.

452
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:05,993
SO FAR.

453
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:07,429
PIE.

454
00:23:07,516 --> 00:23:08,865
[door opens]

455
00:23:10,127 --> 00:23:11,955
OH. BUT YOU'RE--

456
00:23:12,042 --> 00:23:13,957
[door closes]YES, I AM.

457
00:23:14,044 --> 00:23:15,698
SALLY, YOU ALRIGHT?

458
00:23:15,785 --> 00:23:17,134
THIS...

459
00:23:17,221 --> 00:23:21,269
THIS IS PATRICK JANE,
THE MAN WHO SHOT TIM.

460
00:23:21,356 --> 00:23:22,836
[whispers] OH, MY LORD.

461
00:23:22,923 --> 00:23:26,013
DON'T BE SCARED.
I'M HARMLESS, TRULY.

462
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,841
WHAT DO YOU WANT?

463
00:23:27,928 --> 00:23:31,018
I HAD TO TALK TO YOU
FACE-TO-FACE,

464
00:23:31,105 --> 00:23:34,674
SO I'D KNOW FOR SURE.

465
00:23:34,761 --> 00:23:37,198
IF YOUR HUSBAND'S INNOCENT,
IF I MADE A MISTAKE,

466
00:23:37,285 --> 00:23:41,115
THEN I'M TRULY, DEEPLY SORRY,

467
00:23:41,202 --> 00:23:42,856
AND I SWEAR TO YOU,

468
00:23:42,943 --> 00:23:46,076
I WILL SPEND THE REST OF MY LIFE
EARNING YOUR FORGIVENESS.

469
00:23:52,953 --> 00:23:55,651
MR. JANE...

470
00:23:55,738 --> 00:23:57,697
AS GOD IS MY WITNESS,

471
00:23:57,784 --> 00:24:01,048
MY HUSBAND NEVER
BROKE THE LAW IN HIS LIFE.

472
00:24:01,135 --> 00:24:03,267
YOU MURDERED A GOOD MAN.

473
00:24:12,712 --> 00:24:14,801
DO YOU HAVE ANY TEA?

474
00:24:19,675 --> 00:24:20,894
[knocks on door]

475
00:24:20,981 --> 00:24:23,157
MR. DEUTSCH!

476
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:27,596
OPEN IT UP.

477
00:24:28,728 --> 00:24:30,251
YOU GOT A WARRANT?

478
00:24:30,338 --> 00:24:33,036
WE DON'T NEED ONE. WE JUST
WANT A QUICK LOOK AROUND.

479
00:24:33,123 --> 00:24:34,647
LET ME CHECK WITH MY BOSS.

480
00:24:34,734 --> 00:24:35,952
SIR...

481
00:24:36,039 --> 00:24:38,607
WON'T BE LONG.

482
00:24:38,694 --> 00:24:40,435
YOU HEAR THAT?WHAT?

483
00:24:40,522 --> 00:24:42,742
SOUND OF A STRUGGLE, COMING
FROM INSIDE THE APARTMENT.

484
00:24:42,829 --> 00:24:45,005
OH, YEAH. I DO.
SOMEONE MIGHT BE IN DANGER.

485
00:24:45,092 --> 00:24:46,833
YEAH. [grunts]

486
00:25:14,251 --> 00:25:17,080
[Rigsby] HEY. SECURITY GUARD'S
DEAD. HAIR DRYER IN THE BATHTUB.

487
00:25:17,167 --> 00:25:18,429
COULD IT BE AN ACCIDENT?

488
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:20,127
Well, it could be.

489
00:25:20,214 --> 00:25:21,998
EXCEPT THE DEAD GUY'S BALD,
NEAR ENOUGH,

490
00:25:22,085 --> 00:25:24,305
SO WHAT WOULD HE USE
A HAIR DRYER FOR?

491
00:25:24,392 --> 00:25:26,046
LOOKS LIKE SUICIDE OR MURDER.

492
00:25:26,133 --> 00:25:27,613
THAT'S GOOD NEWS.

493
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:30,224
NOT FOR MR. DEUTSCH,
GOD REST HIM,

494
00:25:30,311 --> 00:25:31,442
BUT SUPPORTS JANE'S STORY.

495
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:33,009
Yeah.

496
00:25:33,096 --> 00:25:35,316
SOMEONE MUST'VE ARRANGED
FOR DEUTSCH TO TAKE THE GUN,

497
00:25:35,403 --> 00:25:37,579
SWITCH THE PHONE,
KILLED HIM TO KEEP HIM QUIET.

498
00:25:37,666 --> 00:25:38,928
Be sure that forensics

499
00:25:39,015 --> 00:25:40,626
SEARCH DEUTSCH'S
APARTMENT CAREFULLY.

500
00:25:40,713 --> 00:25:42,149
IT'S A LONG SHOT,

501
00:25:42,236 --> 00:25:45,282
BUT WE MAY GET LUCKY
AND FIND THE GUN OR THE PHONE.

502
00:25:45,369 --> 00:25:48,808
IT'S WEIRD HOW MUCH WE HAD
IN COMMON RIGHT FROM THE START.

503
00:25:48,895 --> 00:25:51,158
WE JUST NATURALLY
MADE A COUPLE.

504
00:25:51,245 --> 00:25:53,029
SOUL MATES.

505
00:25:53,116 --> 00:25:55,031
YES. SOUL MATES.

506
00:25:55,118 --> 00:25:56,990
[knocks]JANE.

507
00:25:57,077 --> 00:26:00,341
OH. [whispers]
EXCUSE ME, PLEASE, SALLY.

508
00:26:00,428 --> 00:26:02,865
[lowered voice] THE FIRST
SECURITY GUARD ON THE SCENE

509
00:26:02,952 --> 00:26:06,913
AFTER THE SHOOTING, IS DEAD--
HAIR-DRYER-IN-THE-BATHTUB DEAD.

510
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,045
WELL, THAT'S A RELIEF.
I MEAN...

511
00:26:09,132 --> 00:26:10,612
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

512
00:26:10,699 --> 00:26:14,442
THIS WOMAN IS GOOD.
STARTING TO DOUBT MY OWN STORY.

513
00:26:14,529 --> 00:26:15,704
TELL ME ABOUT IT.

514
00:26:17,532 --> 00:26:18,620
[clears throat]

515
00:26:18,707 --> 00:26:20,187
[sips] MM.

516
00:26:20,274 --> 00:26:23,190
SALLY, WOULD YOU MIND
IF I USED YOUR BATHROOM?

517
00:26:23,277 --> 00:26:25,496
NOT AT ALL.THANK YOU.

518
00:26:49,216 --> 00:26:52,088
THANK YOU. THAT'S ALL WE NEED.
WE'LL LEAVE YOU IN PEACE.

519
00:26:52,175 --> 00:26:54,177
UH, IN JUST ONE MOMENT.

520
00:26:55,570 --> 00:26:57,790
SEE, THING IS, SALLY,
I LIKE YOU.

521
00:26:57,877 --> 00:27:00,140
I CAN TELL THAT YOU'RE
A GOOD, HONEST PERSON,

522
00:27:00,227 --> 00:27:01,881
WHICH MEANS EITHER I'M CRAZY

523
00:27:01,968 --> 00:27:05,319
OR YOUR HUSBAND WAS KEEPING
SOME VERY DARK SECRETS FROM YOU,

524
00:27:05,406 --> 00:27:07,538
AND I-I'M PRETTY SURE
I'M NOT CRAZY.

525
00:27:07,626 --> 00:27:11,281
MY HUSBAND KEPT
NO SECRETS FROM ME. NONE.

526
00:27:11,368 --> 00:27:14,545
ALL MEN KEEP SECRETS
FROM THEIR WIVES--ALL OF THEM.

527
00:27:14,633 --> 00:27:15,895
TIM WAS NO DIFFERENT.

528
00:27:15,982 --> 00:27:16,939
YOU'RE WRONG.

529
00:27:17,026 --> 00:27:19,594
I BET I CAN PROVE I'M RIGHT.

530
00:27:19,681 --> 00:27:20,987
YOU RECOGNIZE THESE?

531
00:27:21,074 --> 00:27:23,163
YES, OF COURSE--
TIM'S KEY RING.

532
00:27:23,250 --> 00:27:26,122
DO YOU HAVE
YOUR OWN KEYS CLOSE BY?

533
00:27:28,777 --> 00:27:30,474
HOW MANY KEYS
DO YOU HAVE THERE?

534
00:27:30,561 --> 00:27:31,954
UH, SIX.

535
00:27:32,041 --> 00:27:32,999
YOU SURE?

536
00:27:34,522 --> 00:27:37,090
SIX KEYS.

537
00:27:37,177 --> 00:27:39,658
HUH.
YOUR HUSBAND HAS SEVEN.

538
00:27:39,745 --> 00:27:44,967
ONE, TWO, THREE, FOUR,
FIVE, SIX, SEVEN.

539
00:27:45,054 --> 00:27:47,622
WHAT'S THE SEVENTH KEY FOR?

540
00:27:47,709 --> 00:27:49,058
I DON'T KNOW.

541
00:27:49,145 --> 00:27:50,494
YOU DON'T FIND THAT ODD?

542
00:27:51,887 --> 00:27:53,933
NO. I'M SURE LOTS
OF HUSBANDS AND WIVES

543
00:27:54,020 --> 00:27:55,499
HAVE A DIFFERENT
NUMBER OF KEYS.

544
00:27:55,586 --> 00:27:58,111
EXACTLY.
THAT'S WHAT I'M SAYING.

545
00:27:58,198 --> 00:28:00,200
EVERYBODY HAS SECRETS.

546
00:28:00,287 --> 00:28:04,465
THIS IS PROOF POSITIVE THAT
YOUR HUSBAND WAS NO DIFFERENT.

547
00:28:04,552 --> 00:28:06,249
I WONDER WHAT IT OPENS.

548
00:28:07,860 --> 00:28:09,252
YOU THINK YOU'RE SO SMART

549
00:28:09,339 --> 00:28:11,080
WITH THESE LITTLE
MIND GAMES, DON'T YOU?

550
00:28:11,167 --> 00:28:12,473
IT'S JUST A QUESTION.

551
00:28:12,560 --> 00:28:14,388
BUT THE TRUTH IS...

552
00:28:14,475 --> 00:28:18,914
YOU ARE NOTHING BUT A SAD,
CRAZY PERSON, AND A MURDERER.

553
00:28:19,001 --> 00:28:20,524
AND I'M SORRY,

554
00:28:20,611 --> 00:28:23,353
BUT I WANT YOU TO LEAVE
MY HOUSE RIGHT THIS MINUTE.

555
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,528
OKAY.

556
00:28:37,846 --> 00:28:40,022
I DON'T GET WHAT YOU THOUGHT
WAS GONNA HAPPEN.

557
00:28:40,109 --> 00:28:41,807
I WAS FEELING MY WAY.

558
00:28:41,894 --> 00:28:44,157
[sighs] WHAT NOW?

559
00:28:44,244 --> 00:28:45,724
WELL, JUST DRIVE
AROUND THE BLOCK.

560
00:28:45,811 --> 00:28:46,855
OKAY.

561
00:28:46,942 --> 00:28:49,031
WHY?

562
00:28:49,118 --> 00:28:50,990
QUESTION...

563
00:28:51,077 --> 00:28:52,643
DO YOU TRUST ME?

564
00:28:53,993 --> 00:28:56,735
NOT 100%, NO.

565
00:28:56,822 --> 00:28:59,650
DIFFERENT QUESTION, THEN.
OH. COULD YOU STOP RIGHT HERE?

566
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:00,739
[seat belt clicks][sighs]

567
00:29:03,263 --> 00:29:06,527
[groans][car alert beeps]

568
00:29:06,614 --> 00:29:08,398
SO WHAT'S THE QUESTION?[groans]

569
00:29:10,009 --> 00:29:11,140
HOW'S YOUR INJURY?

570
00:29:11,227 --> 00:29:12,228
IT HURTS.

571
00:29:12,315 --> 00:29:14,927
MM. YOU THINK YOU CAN RUN?NO.

572
00:29:15,014 --> 00:29:17,233
YEAH. PROBABLY DON'T
WANT TO GET TOO EXCITED.

573
00:29:17,320 --> 00:29:18,887
YOU'LL POP YOUR STITCHES.WHAT?

574
00:29:18,974 --> 00:29:20,671
I'M GONNA SNEAK
INSIDE THE CARTER HOUSE.

575
00:29:20,759 --> 00:29:22,586
STAY HERE
UNTIL I CALL YOU.DON'T--

576
00:29:22,673 --> 00:29:24,675
DON'T YOU DARE--JANE?

577
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,938
JANE!

578
00:29:26,025 --> 00:29:27,200
[sighs]

579
00:29:46,959 --> 00:29:48,308
[thud]

580
00:29:58,274 --> 00:30:01,843
[indistinct conversations]

581
00:30:25,432 --> 00:30:27,129
[Sally]
THANK YOU FOR COMING.
GOODNIGHT.

582
00:30:27,216 --> 00:30:29,305
[Joan] GOODNIGHT.

583
00:30:29,392 --> 00:30:32,308
IF YOU NEED ME TO STAY OVER,
KEEP YOU COMPANY...

584
00:30:32,395 --> 00:30:34,006
I CAN BABYSIT CHARLAINE.

585
00:30:34,093 --> 00:30:35,050
I'LL BE FINE.

586
00:30:35,137 --> 00:30:36,443
ANYTHING YOU NEED.

587
00:30:36,530 --> 00:30:38,097
THANK YOU, HONEY.
YOU'VE BEEN A ROCK.

588
00:30:38,184 --> 00:30:39,141
[kiss]

589
00:30:39,228 --> 00:30:40,577
CALL ME, OKAY?I WILL.

590
00:30:40,664 --> 00:30:42,623
ALRIGHT. GOODNIGHT.

591
00:30:42,710 --> 00:30:43,885
[creak]

592
00:30:43,972 --> 00:30:45,713
[door closes]

593
00:30:45,800 --> 00:30:47,715
[footsteps approach]

594
00:31:11,260 --> 00:31:12,827
[keys jangle]

595
00:31:15,395 --> 00:31:16,483
[switch clicks]

596
00:31:56,958 --> 00:31:58,481
[keys jangle]

597
00:32:32,037 --> 00:32:35,040
HOW MANY TIMES
DO I HAVE TO SAY IT?

598
00:32:35,127 --> 00:32:37,390
DON'T LOOK AT ME.

599
00:32:41,002 --> 00:32:44,919
DON'T YOU EVER LOOK AT ME.

600
00:32:51,404 --> 00:32:52,883
[sighs]

601
00:32:55,625 --> 00:32:57,236
[drawer closes]

602
00:33:00,543 --> 00:33:03,329
YOU KNOW, DON'T YOU?

603
00:33:06,071 --> 00:33:07,986
YOU KNOW.

604
00:33:12,729 --> 00:33:14,688
[whispers]
WHAT DOES THIS OPEN?

605
00:33:14,775 --> 00:33:16,559
[sniffles]

606
00:33:16,646 --> 00:33:20,520
SHH. OH, DEBBI.

607
00:33:20,607 --> 00:33:23,392
OPEN YOUR EYES.

608
00:33:23,479 --> 00:33:25,003
LOOK AT IT.

609
00:33:27,048 --> 00:33:29,442
WHAT DOES THIS OPEN?

610
00:33:31,139 --> 00:33:33,489
[voice breaking]
I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

611
00:33:33,576 --> 00:33:36,449
YOU LYING SLUT![slap]

612
00:33:36,536 --> 00:33:39,843
YOU AND TIM HAVE BEEN KEEPING
SECRETS FROM ME ALL ALONG,

613
00:33:39,930 --> 00:33:42,324
HAVEN'T YOU? ALL ALONG!

614
00:33:42,411 --> 00:33:44,022
WHAT DOES THIS OPEN?!

615
00:33:45,719 --> 00:33:48,417
IT OPENS MY LOCKER
AT THE CBI GYM.

616
00:33:50,506 --> 00:33:53,683
GOOD NEWS IS, YOUR HUSBAND
WASN'T HIDING ANYTHING FROM YOU.

617
00:33:53,770 --> 00:33:57,209
YOU REALLY WERE SOUL MATES.

618
00:33:57,296 --> 00:33:58,993
BAD NEWS?

619
00:33:59,080 --> 00:34:01,822
YOU'RE UNDER ARREST,
YOU LOONY BITCH.

620
00:34:01,909 --> 00:34:04,085
[Lisbon] OH, MY GOD.

621
00:34:04,172 --> 00:34:08,176
ON YOUR KNEES.
PUT YOUR HANDS ON YOUR HEAD.

622
00:34:08,263 --> 00:34:09,656
[keys clatter]

623
00:34:11,875 --> 00:34:14,530
LISTEN, THIS GIRL IN
THE BASEMENT CHANGES THE GAME.

624
00:34:14,617 --> 00:34:16,358
WE CAN'T APPEAR VINDICTIVE.

625
00:34:16,445 --> 00:34:19,187
JANE HAS AN ENORMOUS AMOUNT
OF PUBLIC SYMPATHY RIGHT NOW.

626
00:34:19,274 --> 00:34:22,756
YEAH, WELL, THE D.A. IS TELLING
ME TO GO FULL SPEED AT HIM.

627
00:34:22,843 --> 00:34:24,366
VIGILANTE JUSTICE
CAN'T GO UNPUNISHED,

628
00:34:24,453 --> 00:34:26,673
REGARDLESS WHAT THE SYMPATHETIC
CIRCUMSTANCES MIGHT BE.

629
00:34:26,760 --> 00:34:28,370
OH, NO, ABSOLUTELY.

630
00:34:28,457 --> 00:34:31,417
A FIRM LINE DRAWN UNDER THIS
EPISODE IS BEST FOR THE BUREAU.

631
00:34:31,504 --> 00:34:34,333
IT WAS BEST FOR ALL CONCERNED.
I'M JUST SAYING...

632
00:34:34,420 --> 00:34:36,422
NO DEATH PENALTY, RIGHT?

633
00:34:36,509 --> 00:34:37,727
NO, THAT'S OUT NOW,

634
00:34:37,814 --> 00:34:39,468
BUT WE ARE CONFIDENT
FIRST DEGREE MURDER

635
00:34:39,555 --> 00:34:40,904
WILL STAND UP.

636
00:34:40,991 --> 00:34:42,993
FACTS DON'T ALLOW
FOR ANY OTHER VERDICT.

637
00:34:43,081 --> 00:34:48,216
AFTER A WHILE,
I STOPPED TRYING TO ESCAPE.

638
00:34:48,303 --> 00:34:51,524
THEN I THOUGHT
ABOUT KILLING MYSELF.

639
00:34:51,611 --> 00:34:54,614
BUT THEN I THOUGHT ABOUT
MY MOM AND DAD AND MY BROTHER,

640
00:34:54,701 --> 00:34:57,356
AND I COULDN'T DO IT.

641
00:34:57,443 --> 00:34:59,880
I HAD TO STAY ALIVE FOR THEM,

642
00:34:59,967 --> 00:35:04,014
SO THAT KEPT A SPARK OF HOPE
ALIVE INSIDE ME.

643
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:06,843
AND THEN, JUST WHEN
I WAS ABOUT TO DESPAIR,

644
00:35:06,930 --> 00:35:09,411
MR. JANE AND AGENT LISBON
CAME AND RESCUED ME.

645
00:35:11,500 --> 00:35:12,980
YOU'RE A BRAVE GIRL, DEBBI.

646
00:35:14,851 --> 00:35:17,637
NOW THAT YOU'VE HAD TIME
TO LOOK BACK CALMLY,

647
00:35:17,724 --> 00:35:19,943
WHAT IS YOUR OPINION
OF TIMOTHY CARTER?

648
00:35:21,423 --> 00:35:23,599
HE'S A MONSTER.

649
00:35:26,646 --> 00:35:29,562
THANK YOU.
NO FURTHER QUESTIONS.

650
00:35:29,649 --> 00:35:31,041
THANK YOU,MR. JANE.

651
00:35:32,521 --> 00:35:34,958
MR. ARDILES?

652
00:35:41,835 --> 00:35:43,141
DEBBI, JUST ONE QUESTION.

653
00:35:45,055 --> 00:35:49,103
DID TIMOTHY CARTER EVER SAY
TO YOU THAT HE WAS RED JOHN?

654
00:35:49,190 --> 00:35:50,539
NO, SIR.

655
00:35:50,626 --> 00:35:52,541
DID HE EVER MENTION
THE NAME RED JOHN?

656
00:35:52,628 --> 00:35:54,761
NO, SIR.

657
00:35:54,848 --> 00:35:57,590
DID HE EVER MENTION ANY OTHER
CRIMES HE MIGHT HAVE COMMITTED?

658
00:35:57,677 --> 00:36:00,984
NO, BUT I DON'T SEE HOW THAT--THANK YOU SO MUCH, DEBBI.

659
00:36:01,071 --> 00:36:02,595
YOU'VE BEEN SUPER HELPFUL.

660
00:36:02,682 --> 00:36:05,772
NO FURTHER QUESTIONS,
YOUR HONOR.

661
00:36:05,859 --> 00:36:07,426
REDIRECT, MR. JANE?

662
00:36:07,513 --> 00:36:08,862
[mouths word]

663
00:36:08,949 --> 00:36:12,735
THE WITNESS MAY STEP DOWN.
THANK YOU, DEBBI.

664
00:36:17,827 --> 00:36:19,177
MR. ARDILES?

665
00:36:22,963 --> 00:36:25,618
NOW MR. JANE

666
00:36:25,705 --> 00:36:27,924
IS GOING TO STAND UP HERE
IN A MOMENT,

667
00:36:28,011 --> 00:36:30,013
AND HE'S GOING TO TELL YOU

668
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:32,929
THAT TIMOTHY CARTER
WAS RED JOHN.

669
00:36:34,931 --> 00:36:38,631
THE FACT IS, HE HAS NO PROOF
OF THAT--NONE WHATSOEVER.

670
00:36:38,718 --> 00:36:42,678
NOW WAS, UH, WAS TIM CARTER
A NICE MAN? NO.

671
00:36:42,765 --> 00:36:43,810
OBVIOUSLY NOT.

672
00:36:45,464 --> 00:36:47,335
BUT WAS HE A SERIAL KILLER?

673
00:36:47,422 --> 00:36:49,859
DO WE HAVE ANY PROOF
THAT HE EVER KILLED ANYONE?

674
00:36:49,946 --> 00:36:52,340
ANYONE AT ALL? NO. WE DON'T.

675
00:36:52,427 --> 00:36:54,168
THE ONLY MURDER THAT WE KNOW OF,

676
00:36:54,255 --> 00:36:56,431
THE ONLY MURDER
THAT IS AN ATTESTED FACT,

677
00:36:56,518 --> 00:37:00,261
IS THE MURDER COMMITTED
BY THIS MAN HERE, PATRICK JANE--

678
00:37:00,348 --> 00:37:02,089
A MURDER COMMITTED

679
00:37:02,176 --> 00:37:05,614
OUT OF MISGUIDED LUST
FOR PERSONAL VENGEANCE.

680
00:37:09,444 --> 00:37:12,273
PROSECUTOR SAYS THAT
TIMOTHY CARTER WASN'T RED JOHN.

681
00:37:12,360 --> 00:37:15,363
WELL, CARTER TOLD ME HIMSELF
THAT HE WASRED JOHN,

682
00:37:15,450 --> 00:37:19,062
BUT I-I CAN'T PROVE THAT.

683
00:37:19,149 --> 00:37:23,589
THE FORENSIC EVIDENCE
IS INCONCLUSIVE.

684
00:37:23,676 --> 00:37:26,679
HIS WIFE REFUSES
TO TALK TO ANYONE,

685
00:37:26,766 --> 00:37:30,857
REFUSES TO SPEAK AT ALL,
SO SHE'S NO USE TO US.

686
00:37:30,944 --> 00:37:33,294
WHAT ABOUT CARTER'S RECORDS?

687
00:37:33,381 --> 00:37:38,168
SURELY THERE MUST BE
SOME CLUES THERE--NO.

688
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:39,735
ON PAPER,

689
00:37:39,822 --> 00:37:44,131
THIS MAN SEEMS TO APPEAR
OUT OF NOWHERE FIVE YEARS AGO.

690
00:37:44,218 --> 00:37:46,699
BEFORE THAT, NOTHING.

691
00:37:46,786 --> 00:37:48,178
WHY?

692
00:37:49,919 --> 00:37:52,531
BECAUSE TIMOTHY CARTER

693
00:37:52,618 --> 00:37:58,232
IS AN INVENTED IDENTITY, A MASK.

694
00:37:58,319 --> 00:38:01,235
I'M NOT GUILTY
OF KILLING TIMOTHY CARTER

695
00:38:01,322 --> 00:38:04,717
BECAUSE TIMOTHY CARTER
NEVER EXISTED.

696
00:38:04,804 --> 00:38:08,982
THERE IS NO TIMOTHY CARTER.
THERE IS ONLY RED JOHN.

697
00:38:11,985 --> 00:38:14,770
RED JOHN...

698
00:38:14,857 --> 00:38:18,644
STARTED KILLING PEOPLE
12 YEARS AGO.

699
00:38:18,731 --> 00:38:22,648
IT'S HARD TO PUT AN EXACT NUMBER
ON HOW MANY PEOPLE HE'S KILLED,

700
00:38:22,735 --> 00:38:27,348
BUT IT'S SOMEWHERE AROUND 28--

701
00:38:27,435 --> 00:38:31,570
NEARLY ALL WOMEN,
LATE AT NIGHT, IN THEIR HOMES.

702
00:38:31,657 --> 00:38:33,311
HE WAKES THEM FIRST,

703
00:38:33,398 --> 00:38:37,271
BECAUSE HE LIKES TO SEE
THE FEAR IN THEIR EYES.

704
00:38:37,358 --> 00:38:41,188
HE LIKES TO HEAR THEM BEG
FOR MERCY AS HE CUTS THEM OPEN.

705
00:38:43,669 --> 00:38:47,542
HE DID THAT
TO MY WIFE AND DAUGHTER...

706
00:38:47,629 --> 00:38:52,112
AND I'VE BEEN LOOKING
FOR HIM EVER SINCE...

707
00:38:52,199 --> 00:38:54,810
LOOKING FOR PERSONAL VENGEANCE.

708
00:38:57,247 --> 00:39:01,643
I BELIEVE THAT'S... MY RIGHT.

709
00:39:01,730 --> 00:39:06,126
I HAVE THE RIGHT TO KILL THE MAN
THAT KILLED MY FAMILY.

710
00:39:06,213 --> 00:39:09,303
I DON'T SAY I SHOULDN'T BE
PUNISHED FOR DOING WHAT I DID.

711
00:39:09,390 --> 00:39:13,176
I FEEL I HAD NO CHOICE.

712
00:39:21,228 --> 00:39:23,491
WHAT WOULD YOU DO?

713
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:41,379
[Van Pelt] ANY NEWS?

714
00:39:41,466 --> 00:39:43,119
THE JURY'S OUT.

715
00:39:43,206 --> 00:39:44,817
HOW'S IT LOOKING?

716
00:39:44,904 --> 00:39:49,256
MAYBE IF WE'RE LUCKY, HE'LL
GIVE HIM SECOND-DEGREE MURDER.

717
00:39:49,343 --> 00:39:51,998
JANE WILL BE OUT OF PRISON
IN THREE OR FOUR YEARS.

718
00:39:52,085 --> 00:39:54,479
[buzzer]

719
00:39:54,566 --> 00:39:59,484
THE JURY'S BACK ALREADY.
THAT CAN'T BE GOOD.

720
00:39:59,571 --> 00:40:01,137
LADIES AND GENTLEMEN
OF THE JURY,

721
00:40:01,224 --> 00:40:03,357
HAVE YOU REACHED
A UNANIMOUS VERDICT?

722
00:40:03,444 --> 00:40:05,751
WE HAVE, YOUR HONOR.

723
00:40:08,231 --> 00:40:11,626
PLEASE STATE YOUR VERDICT
FOR THE COURTROOM.

724
00:40:18,198 --> 00:40:21,506
WE, THE JURY, FIND
THE DEFENDANT, PATRICK JANE...

725
00:40:25,205 --> 00:40:27,250
NOT GUILTY, ON ALL COUNTS.

726
00:40:27,337 --> 00:40:30,210
[gallery murmuring]

727
00:40:34,997 --> 00:40:36,259
[gavel bangs]

728
00:40:36,346 --> 00:40:38,479
QUIET!

729
00:40:38,566 --> 00:40:40,220
[murmuring continues]

730
00:41:13,471 --> 00:41:16,648
SO... WHAT NOW?

731
00:41:16,735 --> 00:41:18,780
NOW?

732
00:41:18,867 --> 00:41:22,262
WELL,
TEA WOULD HIT THE SPOT.

733
00:41:22,349 --> 00:41:24,699
NO. I MEAN, WHAT NOW?

734
00:41:24,786 --> 00:41:27,267
WELL, YOU'VE DONE WHAT
YOU SET OUT TO DO.

735
00:41:27,354 --> 00:41:29,617
YOU GOT YOUR VENGEANCE.

736
00:41:29,704 --> 00:41:33,360
DO YOU FEEL DIFFERENT?
FEEL BETTER?

737
00:41:33,447 --> 00:41:35,797
NO. I FEEL GUILTY.

738
00:41:35,884 --> 00:41:37,233
GUILTY? WHY?

739
00:41:37,320 --> 00:41:39,932
FOR DECEIVING THE JURY.
I MEAN, I HAD NO CHOICE.

740
00:41:40,019 --> 00:41:41,237
GOING TO PRISON FOR MURDER

741
00:41:41,324 --> 00:41:44,110
WOULD HAVE BEEN
A VICTORY FOR RED JOHN.

742
00:41:44,197 --> 00:41:46,678
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?
RED JOHN'S DEAD.

743
00:41:46,765 --> 00:41:48,375
TIMOTHY CARTER'S DEAD.

744
00:41:48,462 --> 00:41:50,943
HE WAS AN EVIL MAN,
BUT HE WASN'T RED JOHN.

745
00:41:51,030 --> 00:41:53,075
RED JOHN...

746
00:41:53,162 --> 00:41:54,686
IS STILL ALIVE.

747
00:41:56,470 --> 00:41:58,603
WATCH THE ROAD.

